## torrc — TorService (auto-installed via NSSM)
## Tor SOCKS Proxy v2.0 with Snowflake support

# --- Data / logging (relative paths resolved by NSSM AppDirectory) ---
DataDirectory data
Log notice file logs/tor-notice.log

# GeoIP files are OPTIONAL — only needed for country-based node filtering
# (ExcludeNodes/ExcludeExitNodes). Uncomment these two lines only if you
# copied geoip/geoip6 into the install directory (from the Expert Bundle's
# Data\Tor folder).
#GeoIPFile geoip
#GeoIPv6File geoip6

# --- SOCKS proxy ---
# Loopback-only by default. SocksPort is bound to 127.0.0.1, which means
# EVERY connecting client's address is seen by Tor as 127.0.0.1 - so
# 127.0.0.1 must be explicitly accepted, or nothing can ever connect.
#
# To share on LAN instead, change SocksPort to 0.0.0.0:9050 - only then
# will real 192.168.x.x client addresses show up and the second accept
# line below becomes meaningful.
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050
SocksPolicy accept 127.0.0.1/32
SocksPolicy accept 192.168.0.0/16
SocksPolicy reject *

# --- Control port (local-only, for WebSocket API) ---
# ControlSocket runs on a named pipe for local process communication.
# The WebSocket API server connects to this for Tor status and commands.
ControlPort 127.0.0.1:9051
CookieAuthentication 1
CookieAuthFilePortReadable 1

# --- Bridges (OPTIONAL, off by default) ---
# A plain SOCKS proxy doesn't need bridges unless this machine's direct Tor
# connections are being blocked (e.g. Iran's DPI). Bridges are NOT baked
# into this file anymore - they age out fast and shipping one specific
# person's bridge lines to every install is neither useful nor something
# other users need. Instead:
#
#   Drop a *.conf file into bridges.d\ containing UseBridges 1,
#   ClientTransportPlugin ..., and your own Bridge lines, then
#   `nssm restart TorService`. Tor picks it up automatically via the
#   %include below - no torrc edits needed, and if bridges.d\ is empty
#   this line is silently a no-op (glob %include with zero matches is not
#   an error in Tor - a literal missing filename would be).
#
# See bridges.d\README.txt for the exact format. Ready-to-use examples
# ship as bridges.d\*.conf.sample files - rename them (drop the .sample)
# to activate those specific bridges.
#
# Supported transports: obfs4, webtunnel, snowflake
%include bridges.d/*.conf
